y}^{′}$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-331373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe predictor equation of the modified Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p}={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initially predicted new $y$-value is then given by ${y}_{p}=y+Δ{y}_{p}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the value of ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} \\\\  & ={0}^{2}+2\\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δ{y}_{p}$ using the predictor equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this value to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ |  |\n\nHence, according to the predictor equation, the initially predicted new $y$-value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =y+Δ{y}_{p} \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $2$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-331373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7aca546a0d56627f8183bfb2c9d1a3326c8353f0cfd18d4a316ca3ae787d559b"} {"question" "q-331373" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-331373" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-331373" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-331373" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-331373" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-331373" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-330781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x+y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using the modified Euler method. Given that the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2},$ fill the missing entries in the table below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-330781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe predictor equation of the modified Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p}={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initially predicted new $y$-value is then given by ${y}_{p}=y+Δ{y}_{p}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the value of ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2x+y \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δ{y}_{p}$ using the predictor equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{y}_{p} & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this value to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |\n\nHence, according to the predictor equation, the initially predicted new $y$-value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =y+Δ{y}_{p} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $Δ{y}_{p}$ | ${y}_{p}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-330781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7aca546a0d56627f8183bfb2c9d1a3326c8353f0cfd18d4a316ca3ae787d559b"} {"question" "q-330781" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-330781" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044701/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f50c06d597587ef706912ea9b536f4809b023367657ba94056973d20089442d"} {"question" "q-330781" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answe